From: MahanHD <mahanheidari2003@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] read a BlackLevel per camera

Nothing told an application the sensor's black level, so Megapixels
guessed one from the preview, nudging it until a few percent of pixels
were black. That number depends on the scene: in a dim one it overshot
the IMX200's real pedestal of 64 and ate most of the blue channel's
signal, which drove auto white balance to three times too much blue gain.

Add an optional BlackLevel key to the camera section, on the 16-bit scale
libcamera's tuning files use, appended to libmegapixels_camera.

---
--- a/docs/config.rst	2026-10-12 23:47:34.111548953 +0400
+++ b/docs/config.rst	2026-10-12 23:47:48.259770401 +0400
@@ -95,6 +95,9 @@
 * :code:`FlashPath`: optional, defines the path to a LED device to use as the flash for this camera.
 * :code:`FlashDisplay`: optional, defines that there is no LED that can be used as flash, use the display as the
   light-source instead.
+* :code:`BlackLevel`: optional, the raw value of zero light (the sensor's pedestal) on a 16-bit scale, the way
+  libcamera's tuning files give it: 4096 for a 10-bit sensor whose pedestal is 64. Applications subtract it before
+  white balance and store it in DNG files.
 
 The camera section requires a :code:`SensorDriver` and :code:`BridgeDriver` key. The BridgeDriver will identify the bridge device (eg.
 /dev/video0) and media device (eg. /dev/media0). This combination should uniquely identify a single camera on the device.
--- a/include/libmegapixels.h	2026-10-12 23:47:34.111754123 +0400
+++ b/include/libmegapixels.h	2026-10-12 23:47:48.259401535 +0400
@@ -105,6 +105,9 @@
 
 		int num_handles;
 		libmegapixels_subdev **handles;
+
+		// Raw value of zero light on a 16-bit scale, 0 when not configured
+		int black_level;
 };
 typedef struct _lmp_camera libmegapixels_camera;
 
--- a/src/parse.c	2026-10-12 23:47:34.111814636 +0400
+++ b/src/parse.c	2026-10-12 23:47:48.259596143 +0400
@@ -253,6 +253,7 @@
 	camera->name = strdup(name);
 	camera->sensor_name = strdup(sensor_driver);
 	camera->bridge_name = strdup(bridge_driver);
+	config_setting_lookup_int(root, "BlackLevel", &camera->black_level);
 	config->cameras = realloc(config->cameras, (config->count + 1) * sizeof(config->cameras));
 	if (config->cameras == NULL) {
 		return -1;
